Hi everyone,

It occurred to me, that ther is something wrong with polymorphing 
into this powerful monster or that vampire lord etc. Imagine the
situation:
Hikaru the Samurai (utterly lawful) has shown his devotion to the
lawful gods by always staying on the right path, sacrificing to 
his god, and contributing to the church (which is always in sore
need of these extra few gold pieces). He was in turn rewarded by 
gaining intrinsic protection.  Now Hikaru finds out, that he can 
polymorph, and soon chooses the form of a Vampire Lord.
Oh ultimate crime!
Oh shameful offence!
But it seems, that the gods still protect him...

I propose that polymorphing into any monster not of one's alignment
should result in a major offence to one's god, effectively removing
intrinsic protection, good graces, and possibly (Maybe a little 
harsh, but the gods ain't so lenient in these troubled times anymore!)
destroy the artifacts, that you got from your god.

Well?

